    <forecast>
        <area aac="SA_FA001" description="South Australia" type="region">
            <forecast-period start-time-local="2026-11-20T21:18:45+10:30" end-time-local="2026-11-20T21:18:45+10:30" start-time-utc="2026-11-20T10:48:45Z" end-time-utc="2026-11-20T10:48:45Z">
                <text type="warning_summary_footer">For latest warnings go to www.bom.gov.au, subscribe to RSS feeds, call 1300 659 210* or listen for warnings on relevant TV and radio broadcasts.</text>
                <text type="synoptic_situation">A low pressure trough about eastern South Australia moves east to clear the state Friday evening. A weak high pressure system about the west moves across the state on Saturday. A trough of low pressure and cold front move into the west late Saturday evening and cross the remainder of of South Australia on Sunday. Another cold front clips the southeast on Monday, followed by a high pressure system, which will then move across southern parts of the state on Tuesday.</text>
                <text type="product_footer">* Calls to 1300 numbers cost around 27.5c incl. GST, higher from mobiles or public phones.</text>
            </forecast-period>
        </area>
        <area aac="SA_PW011" description="Eastern Eyre Peninsula" type="public-district" parent-aac="SA_FA001">
            <forecast-period index="0" start-time-local="2026-11-20T21:00:00+10:30" end-time-local="2026-11-21T00:00:00+10:30" start-time-utc="2026-11-20T10:30:00Z" end-time-utc="2026-11-20T13:30:00Z">
                <text type="forecast">Clear. Winds west to southwesterly 15 to 25 km/h.</text>
            </forecast-period>
            <forecast-period index="1" start-time-local="2026-11-21T00:00:00+10:30" end-time-local="2026-11-22T00:00:00+10:30" start-time-utc="2026-11-20T13:30:00Z" end-time-utc="2026-11-21T13:30:00Z">
                <text type="forecast">The chance of fog in the early morning. Mostly sunny day. The chance of a thunderstorm in the south at night. Light winds becoming north to northeasterly 20 to 30 km/h in the morning. Overnight temperatures falling to between 11 and 15 with daytime temperatures reaching the mid to high 30s.</text>
                <text type="fire_danger">High</text>
                <text type="uv_alert">Sun protection 9:00am to 5:10pm, UV Index predicted to reach 11 [Extreme]</text>
            </forecast-period>
            <forecast-period index="2" start-time-local="2026-11-22T00:00:00+10:30" end-time-local="2026-11-23T00:00:00+10:30" start-time-utc="2026-11-21T13:30:00Z" end-time-utc="2026-11-22T13:30:00Z">
                <text type="forecast">Medium chance of showers in the morning and early afternoon. The chance of a thunderstorm in the morning and early afternoon. Mostly sunny afternoon. Winds northerly 20 to 30 km/h shifting west to southwesterly 25 to 35 km/h early in the morning. Overnight temperatures falling to between 19 and 23 with daytime temperatures reaching the low 30s.</text>
            </forecast-period>
            <forecast-period index="3" start-time-local="2026-11-23T00:00:00+10:30" end-time-local="2026-11-24T00:00:00+10:30" start-time-utc="2026-11-22T13:30:00Z" end-time-utc="2026-11-23T13:30:00Z">
                <text type="forecast">Mostly sunny. Winds west to southwesterly 15 to 25 km/h tending south to southwesterly 25 to 40 km/h during the day. Overnight temperatures falling to around 12 with daytime temperatures reaching the mid to high 20s.</text>
            </forecast-period>
            <forecast-period index="4" start-time-local="2026-11-24T00:00:00+10:30" end-time-local="2026-11-25T00:00:00+10:30" start-time-utc="2026-11-23T13:30:00Z" end-time-utc="2026-11-24T13:30:00Z">
                <text type="forecast">Cloud clearing. Winds southeast to southwesterly 15 to 25 km/h tending east to southeasterly 15 to 20 km/h during the morning then tending south to southeasterly 15 to 25 km/h during the afternoon. Overnight temperatures falling to between 8 and 12 with daytime temperatures reaching 22 to 27.</text>
            </forecast-period>
        </area>
